# B's pivot-addressing resolution
#
# Transposed B makes K's own stride ldb-sized (= N * element size) instead
# of element-sized, which changes how iterator_stream_t::try_plan_nd
# resolves K's pivot chain as N grows -- these two shapes pin down that
# resolution at opposite ends: multi_ntile_init lands K's pivot axis in the
# single-pivot-register branch (regression case for a real corruption bug,
# fixed by iterator_nd_t::emit_init_() only running an axis's own init step
# on its first visit), multi_strip lands it in the multi-strip chain with a
# materialized inter-pivot stride instead.
--reset
--transB=1
64x64x32_n"transb_pivot_multi_ntile_init"

--reset
--transB=1
64x128x32_n"transb_pivot_multi_strip"
